ethercat (1:1.6.9-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix PREOP scan using a stale datagram pointer (mika/dev-1.6
    0565b558). The slave-scan FSM could dereference a datagram pointer
    that had already been freed/reused, breaking PREOP scanning on
    affected setups. Reported by GameOEver as
    linuxcnc-ethercat/linuxcnc-ethercat#494 -- thanks for the report;
    the root cause was in the EtherCAT master driver, not the
    linuxcnc-ethercat HAL component.

 -- Luca Toniolo <toniolo.luca@gmail.com>  Mon, 20 Jul 2026 16:25:00 +0800

ethercat (1:1.6.9-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * ethercat-dkms: depend on autoconf, automake, libtool and pkg-config.
    dkms.conf MAKE[0] runs `./bootstrap` (autoreconf) before configure,
    but the autotools were only in source Build-Depends, not in the dkms
    package's runtime Depends. On a clean machine the on-target DKMS
    build (install time / kernel-postinst) failed with:
        ./bootstrap: line 32: autoreconf: command not found
        # exit code: 127
    so ec_master was never built and ethercat.service failed to start
    with "Module ec_master not found". Pull the build tools in so apt
    installs them alongside the dkms package.

 -- Luca Toniolo <toniolo.luca@gmail.com>  Mon, 22 Jun 2026 10:33:12 +0800

ethercat (1:1.6.9-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix DKMS build failure on epoch-versioned packages. dpkg version
    `1:1.6.9-1+deb13u1` was being used verbatim as DKMS PACKAGE_VERSION
    and as the /usr/src/ethercat-<VERSION> path. Kernel Makefile rejects
    `:` in module directory paths:
        Makefile:152: *** module directory path cannot contain ':'. Stop.
    Strip the optional `N:` epoch prefix in debian/rules, postinst, and
    prerm before extracting the upstream version.

 -- Luca Toniolo <toniolo.luca@gmail.com>  Mon, 18 May 2026 21:00:00 +0000

ethercat (1:1.6.9-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First non-pre release of the linuxcnc-ethercat fork of IgH
    EtherLab. Carries the cumulative work from the
    1.6.9+parallelop1~preN series:
    - Inline parallel-op TX queue (mika/dev-1.6 base) cuts cold-start
      DC sync time and quiets the steady-state
      "Failed to get reference clock time: I/O error" warning storm
      via dc_offset_valid + EIO/ENXIO/EAGAIN whitelist.
    - CI matrix builds for Debian 11/12/13 and Ubuntu 22.04/24.04;
      tagged releases publish to linuxcnc-ethercat/apt.
  * Versioned with Debian epoch (1:) so this package cleanly
    upgrades over the openSUSE EtherLab build
    (ethercat-master 1.6.9.gb709e58-1+28.1), which would otherwise
    sort higher than a plain 1.6.9-1.

 -- Luca Toniolo <toniolo.luca@gmail.com>  Tue, 12 May 2026 12:00:00 +0000

ethercat (1.6.9+parallelop1~pre9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rebased on mika/dev-1.6 to silence the user-visible
    "Failed to get reference clock time: Input/output error" warning:
    - Port Synapticon's dc_offset_valid flag (B-base-02 partial):
      kernel returns -EAGAIN instead of -EIO while the per-slave DC
      offset write loop is still in progress, killing the cold-start
      storm.
    - Whitelist EIO/ENXIO/EAGAIN in libethercat
      ecrt_master_reference_clock_time() wrapper so steady-state
      polling races (sync_datagram queued but reply not yet RECEIVED)
      no longer spam stderr at 1-4 kHz cyclic rates. Return value
      still propagates so callers keep their valid/invalid flag
      semantics.

 -- Luca Toniolo <toniolo.luca@gmail.com>  Wed, 06 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

