ethercat (1.6.9+parallelop1~pre5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship udev rule (99-EtherCAT.rules) granting group "ethercat" access
    to /dev/EtherCAT* devices.
  * Create system group "ethercat" on install; remove on purge.
  * postinst prints reminder to add user to the ethercat group.
  * Rebased on Mika's dev-1.6 (FSM/EC_IO_TIMEOUT work, distro-tagged
    release artefacts).
  * Build all common NIC drivers in the DKMS module (8139too, e100,
    e1000, e1000e, r8169, igb, igc, genet) instead of only igc.
  * CI now produces a parallel "eoe" variant of every package
    (ethercat-master-eoe, libethercat-eoe, libethercat-eoe-dev,
    ethercat-dkms-eoe) with --enable-eoe set. The two variants
    Conflict with each other so only one can be installed at a time.

